-- NEGATIVE fixture for R12 (spec §15.12): rule-date-REBINDING decides are not
-- emitted.
--
-- `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` evaluates a sub-graph under its OWN rule
-- date. A DMN DRG has one global rule-date input and no scoped rebinding, so
-- no faithful <decision> exists for such a decide: it is dropped by the
-- population filter (§2.5.6's new structural rule), and the D-RULEDATE-UNBOUND
-- note — now Lossy, not Blocking — says so from the population side.
--
-- Four decides, each pinning one edge of the rule:
--
--   * `the fee under the 2016 rules`         the plain rebind, DROPPED;
--   * `twice the 2016 fee`                   its surviving CALLER: it stays
--                                            emitted, and the dropped callee
--                                            surfaces as an ordinary inputData
--                                            (no dangling requiredDecision);
--   * `the fee under the 2019 rules, doubled` the rebind hidden in a WHERE
--                                            local — the population predicate
--                                            runs over the RAW body, and this
--                                            pins that it sees through WHERE
--                                            exactly as the old peeled-body
--                                            detection did;
--   * `the fixture-shaped rebind`            ALSO satisfies FIXTURE(a)-(c)
--                                            module-locally (referenced only
--                                            from a directive argument, no
--                                            callers, never the tested
--                                            subject) — it must carry ONE drop
--                                            reason (the rebind) and no
--                                            D-FIXTURE advisory, even when the
--                                            importer view is unavailable.
--
-- NEVER added to `goldenSubjects`. Asserted from jl4/tests/DmnExport.hs.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

§ `rule-date rebinding`

TIMEZONE IS "Asia/Singapore"

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the fee` MEANS
    IF `RULES EFFECTIVE DATE` AT LEAST Date 1 1 2024 THEN 9 ELSE 3

-- The plain rebind. Dropped (D-RULEDATE-UNBOUND, Lossy).
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the fee under the 2016 rules` MEANS
    `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (Date 1 9 2016) `the fee`

-- Its surviving caller. Kept; the dropped callee becomes an inputData.
GIVETH A NUMBER
`twice the 2016 fee` MEANS
    `the fee under the 2016 rules` TIMES 2

-- The WHERE-wrapped rebind. Dropped by the same raw-body predicate.
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the fee under the 2019 rules, doubled` MEANS
    pinned TIMES 2
    WHERE
        pinned MEANS `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (Date 1 6 2019) `the fee`

-- The fixture-crossing case: referenced only from the directive argument
-- position below, no callers, never the tested subject — FIXTURE(a)-(c) —
-- AND a rebind. The rebind drop must win, alone.
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the fixture-shaped rebind` MEANS
    `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (Date 1 9 2016) `the fee`

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`double` n MEANS n TIMES 2

#EVAL `double` `the fixture-shaped rebind`
